findings.what:
The crowns are clusters of flat-coloured polygon plates with straight edges. At 11 m the plates are plainly untextured. At 28.5 m they read as a stylized papercraft canopy that is consistent and readable.

Every measurable item in the r12 M11 fix spec passes:
- gloss 0;
- a gradient;
- 20+ jittered plates;
- sway ≤ 4 cm;
- canopy p50 51–56 and p99 91–95;
- brush bend and no leak.

WORLD.md:62 specifies 'instanced bevelled plates, no alpha cards'. What is left is the 'painted edges hide the geometry' half of the LoL bar.
